---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import shot from '../assets/screens/app-power-history.png';
---

<section class="section section--alt" id="history" aria-labelledby="history-title">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="split__copy" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">History and insights</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="history-title">See how your power use changes over time.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        MacPUMP keeps a private record on your Mac, so you can look back at the last hour, yesterday or last week and
        see what your Mac actually used.
      </p>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>
          <strong>From 15 minutes to 30 days.</strong> Energy used, average, peak and minimum, with a chart and an
          average line.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Battery history and a health trend,</strong> so you can see how your battery is ageing.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>A resting-power estimate:</strong> roughly what your Mac uses when it’s doing very little.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gaps stay gaps.</strong> When your Mac was asleep or off, the chart is left blank and never counted as
          0 W.
        </li>
        <li><strong>A weekly report and CSV export</strong> of every history, ready for Numbers or Excel.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="caption history__note">
        History is kept for 7 days by default, or 30 if you choose. Recording can be turned off, and you can delete it at
        any time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="split__media" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:80ms">
      <figure>
        <div class="app-shot">
          <Image
            src={shot}
            alt="The MacPUMP dashboard, Power History tab, for the last 6 hours: cards for energy used 24.9 Wh, average power 13.1 W, highest 38.2 W and lowest 1.7 W, a power-over-time chart of Mac, adapter and battery power with gaps left blank, and an energy-used bar chart."
            widths={[480, 800, 1200, 1600]}
            sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 560px"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="caption">
          Power History over six hours. The blank stretch is when no data was recorded; it isn’t counted as 0 W.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .history__note {
    margin-top: var(--s-5);
  }
</style>
